   "meta": {
    "application": "BambuStudio-01.10.01.50",
    "profile_title": "Pig Pens for Pig Hole - Board Game (KR_Design edition)",
    "profile_notes": "0.4mm nozzle, 0.2mm layers, 2 walls, 15% grid infill, includes modifiers for honeycomb floor, no supports. Printed in Bambu PLA Wood - Black Walnut. Great model and great game! The family kept knocking the little squealers all over the place during gameplay so I created some Pig Pens to keep them under control during the game (pens for the pigs, not for the kids - not yet anyways!). The pens hold your pigs during the game and are stored in the original designer's game box with no modifications. There are 6 pens in all, 5 outer pens which are all identical, and 1 inner pen. The inner pen has a cover plate to be put in place (from the inside of the pen) when taken out of the box and removed again when storing the pens in the box. The pen floors are mesh honeycomb for easy clean-up! The model print profiles include modifiers that eliminate the top and bottom surfaces to create the open honeycomb floor. The build plate for the outer pig pens has all 5 pens; if for some reason you need to print fewer than 5, be sure to include the corresponding modifier with its pen to get the honeycomb floor. The second build plate has the inner pen and cover plate, each with their own modifiers. A1 Mini users - the assembly of 5 Outer Pig Pens on build plate 1 is just a hair too big to fit, you can delete one of the pens and its modifier to get it to fit, you just have to also print one on its own. Thanks again to KR_Design for sharing the original game.",
